 "method": "Walk-forward projection accuracy, 2023-25 regular season (Props Modeler, 2026-11-14).\nEach game is predicted only with data from before it:\n- Features: data/features/player_games.parquet via common.prep (all rolling features are shift(1)).\n- Mean model: stats-only baseline (Poisson GLM, train_backtest.Baseline) per market, refit EVERY WEEK on an expanding\n  window (all labeled eligible rows from seasons < S plus weeks < w of season S), then predicts week w.\n- Level-drift correction: train_backtest.bias_factor on the out-of-sample prediction stream (strictly earlier weeks,\n  17-week window, warmed up with 2022 out-of-sample predictions).\n- Distribution: family = the one backtest_results.json picked for that variant (chosen on 2024; noted as a caveat);\n  dispersion / empirical ratios for season S fitted only on season S-1 out-of-sample predictions (model trained on < S-1).\n- Projection = median of that distribution; range = [p25, p75]; counts use integer quantiles.\n- Live variant per market (where it differs): baseline_market / ml_market refit weekly the same way (ML with the\n  backtest's fixed iteration count); frozen v2 volume x efficiency (rush_yds, rec_yds) scored as-is on 2024-25 only\n  (it was trained on 2018-23, so 2023 is in-sample and excluded; not refit).\nBenchmarks: season-to-date average (prior games this season; if < 2 prior games this season, prior-season average;\nif no prior-season games either, all prior games), last-8 EWMA (<y>_ewm8, shift(1)). No historical sportsbook lines\nexist for 2023-25 in our data, so mae_line = null.\nWrites models/projection_accuracy.json. Nothing live is touched.",
